[Music]  this year the holiday shopping struggle  has been real more tech products have  either been sold out or have longer wait  times than usual but after several  failed attempts to place an order i  finally got one of the hot ticket items  on my list  a nintendo switch so what helped me get  it inventory tracking apps  inventory tracking apps send users  alerts across a wide range of retailers  so think amazon walmart target for  example on top of typical holiday  shortages that we see this time of year  due to increased demand this year we're  dealing with an ongoing computer chip  crisis which hurt inventory levels last  holiday season and it's bleeding into  this one that's a big reason why a lot  of these products have either been sold  out or out of stock for months now in  fact adobe analytics data says that  shoppers saw more than 2 billion out of  stock messages this holiday season and  that's a 325 rise over pre-pandemic  levels and it probably won't get better  for months now or maybe even longer i  can't sit there and manually refresh  everything it's just impossible so you  use the tools at hand and that's what  people do that's justin vavrick and he  created nowinstock.net one of many  websites that send inventory tracking  alerts he says there are two main ways  for tracker sites to know when an item  is in stock one is to partner with a  retailer to tap into its website code  also known as its application  programming interface or api api is  basically like you're making a request  to a database  and you receive an answer you say i want  the information about this product and  it returns you a predetermined  set of values and you can use those  values to  determine whether an item's in stock and  like justin's site other platforms use  similar methods to find in-demand  products another way sites find in-stock  items is with a scraper tool which  periodically checks a retailer's website  for subtle changes those can be tweaks  in its url or other not so obvious  changes to online shoppers scrapers can  also pick up if a website banner changes  from out of stock to in stock or from  out of stock to add to cart then  algorithms can let users know what's  available the content directorate  brickseek another stock monitoring  platform told me that the company  monitors inventory nationally and checks  product codes locally to help people  find the items that they're after even  if it's not something that we're  necessarily notified of proactively our  system in the background is constantly  24 7  checking and rechecking across the  nation all of those different products  in our product catalog constantly  updating the information about what  those price points are so after hearing  about all these apps and websites i  realized i needed to create accounts so  i made an account with hot stock and zoo  alert trying to place an order for a ps5  which i'm still actually trying to get  and a nintendo switch while initially i  was getting alerts for both of them  quite often i've only been able to get  the nintendo switch pretty quickly into  the process i realized that the biggest  limitation was actually me i just  couldn't pull the trigger fast enough to  place the order experts tell me that  that's largely because i'm competing  against automated buying bots which  scoop in and buy up all the merchandise  faster than humans can and they resell  the merchandise on websites like amazon  and ebay but for more money the problem  lies in the fact that  they're so quick  that  when there's enough of them running they  can basically snap up all the inventory  with that problem in mind i started  reaching out to people online who got  the items that i was after but by using  inventory tracking apps and websites  that's how i found maurice who used hot  stock to find a ps5 as soon as the link  came up on my hot stock app i clicked on  it it took me to you know the walmart  app and then it automatically loaded up  the uh the ps5 actually something  similar happened to me it took several  failed attempts before i was able to add  a nintendo switch to my cart i just  couldn't add it fast enough it happened  early one morning i got a random  notification from hot stock saying go to  gamestop's website and that the nintendo  switch was in stock so i went to the  website was able to add it to cart and  check out without a problem a week later  the box arrived on my doorstep here are  some tips on how to get inventory  tracking apps to work better for you  number one if you're using one of these  turn on your alerts including the  notifications on your smartphone two  turn on your sound overnight if your  phones on vibrate when retailers are  updating their stock at midnight or  later you won't hear those alerts  hotstock for example can send a push  notification to your web browser while  nowinstock.net might send you a push  notification on your smartphone or a  text message three be open to using  multiple devices sometimes your  smartphone might get a notification and  show it to you faster than your laptop  for instance and maybe your laptop gets  that notification faster than your  desktop computer it all depends oh and  if your phone is on low power mode turn  that off sometimes that slows down how  quickly your notifications might pop up  on your smartphone and if it's paired  with your apple watch it might slow down  how quickly you see that notification on  your watch four create accounts with all  the major retailers selling the item  that you're after or that would be  selling it if it wasn't sold out the  checkout process runs a lot smoother if  the retailer already has your credit  card information your name and phone  number so make sure you enter all of  that information in the app before you  even start and lastly be diligent it's  gonna take a couple tries before you get  the item that you want unless you're  really lucky or unless you hire someone  to create some bots for you  if you guys are on this mission or have  gotten the items that you're after using  inventory tracking apps comment below  and let me know also be sure to  subscribe to stay up to date on all the  latest tech gadgets and the industry  that's powering them until next time  [Music]

